## 3. Remaining Work

### High Priority

#### 3.1 UI Integration Gaps (22 items)
- `MinimapRenderer` class exists but not integrated into `gui.py` layout
- `highlight_move_range()` exists but not called during unit movement
- `highlight_attack_range()` exists but not called during combat
- Zoom level display/controls in UI (mouse wheel works but no buttons)
- Resource trend arrows (↑↓→) not implemented
- Resource details on hover for resource bar
- Trade route yield display in resource bar
- Resource surplus/deficit indicators
- Color-coded events (all same color)
- Event action buttons
- Event filtering
- Full toolbar icon set (empty by default)

#### 3.2 Economy & Resources
- External trade routes with other civilizations via merchant units
- Gold management (unit maintenance, tribute, bribery)
- Tax system (tax rates, effects on happiness/gold)
- Market simulation (resource scarcity affects prices)

#### 3.3 Happiness & Stability
- Happiness system (luxury resources, entertainment buildings, overextension penalty)
- Stability system (decreases with wars, succession, conquest)
- Happiness effects (production loss, rebellion risk, growth slowdown)
- Stability effects (growth speed, rebellion chance, tax efficiency)

### Medium Priority

#### 4.1 Faction System
- Nobles, Religious, Popular faction types
- Faction pressure affecting stability and succession
- Faction support for claimants during succession

#### 4.2 Plots & Intrigue (Partially Implemented)
- Plot types (assassination, coup, rebellion, poisoning)
- Plot participants with hidden motives and detection
- Spy network with operations
- Counter-intelligence (spymaster bonuses, double agents)
- Plot consequences (imprisonment, exile)

#### 4.3 Events & Narrative
- Event chains (multi-part storylines)
- Event choices with consequences
- Historical scenarios for different eras
- Narrative log with filtering
- Character/city/world events

### Low Priority

#### 5.1 AI Improvements
- AI personality types (aggressive, diplomatic, economic, scholarly)
- Difficulty levels

#### 5.2 Civilizations
- 8-12 unique civs with bonuses, unique units/buildings
- Preferred governments per civ
- Starting terrain preferences

#### 5.3 End Game
- Dynasty victory (survive X generations)
- End-game screen with stats and dynasty tree
- Victory stats summary

#### 5.4 Polish (Quick Wins)
- Keyboard shortcuts (1-8 for toolbar)
- Right-click context menu
- "Next Turn" confirmation dialog
- Game speed options (1x, 2x, 5x)
- Sound toggle
- Unit movement preview
- Combat difficulty modifier
- City name customization
- Music system
- Multiple save slots / auto-save
- Game scenarios (Classic, Historical, Custom)

## 4. Known Issues & Technical Debt

1. **Import conflicts:** `city.py` imported by both `simulation.py` and `game.py` — verify no circular imports
2. **Unit names:** Named by type (e.g., "Militia") not unique — should use UUID or indexed names
3. **Map coordinate system:** Uses (x, y) but hex logic uses axial (q, r) — verify consistency in `hex_map.py`
4. **Economy calculations:** Gold/science/culture in `economy.py` may not match city yields in `city.py`
5. **Combat:** Simple random roll — no terrain/deployment bonuses fully integrated
6. **AI:** Framework in place but limited logic
7. **GUI:** tkinter-based — consider migrating to pygame/arcade for better performance
8. **City growth:** `city_growth.py` exists but may not be fully integrated into the main game loop
9. **Plot system:** Partially implemented, needs completion
10. **Sound/visual effects:** Stubbed, needs real implementation

## 5. Implementation Priority Matrix

| Priority | Task | Complexity | Impact |
|------|------|------|------|
| P0 | Fix UI integration gaps (minimap, highlighting, zoom) | Low | High |
| P0 | Fix economy/city yield mismatch | Medium | High |
| P0 | Complete happiness/stability system | Medium | High |
| P1 | Complete plot/intrigue system | Medium | Medium |
| P1 | Add event chains and choices | Medium | Medium |
| P1 | Quick wins (keyboard shortcuts, context menu, etc.) | Low | Medium |
| P2 | AI personality/difficulty | High | Medium |
| P2 | 8-12 unique civilizations | High | Medium |
| P3 | End-game screen and dynasty victory | Medium | Low |
| P3 | Consider pygame migration | High | Low |

## 6. Recommendations

1. **Fix critical integration gaps first** (P0): The minimap, highlighting, and economy calculations are blocking features that users will immediately notice.
2. **Complete happiness/stability** (P0): This is a core Civ mechanic that's missing and affects gameplay depth.
3. **Implement quick wins** (P1-P2): These are low-effort, high-impact improvements that will make the game feel more polished.
4. **Add faction system** (P1): This adds political depth and complements the existing dynasty system.
5. **Complete plot/intrigue** (P1): The stub is in place; fleshing it out adds narrative richness.
6. **Expand civilizations** (P2): 8-12 civs with unique bonuses will make the game more replayable.
7. **Consider pygame migration** (P3): tkinter works but pygame would provide better performance and visual capabilities.

